+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+Domain code in `src/domain/` returns a `Result` and never throws. `add`, `rename` and `tag` currently accept any text; `createTask`, `renameTask` and `addTag` in `task.ts` are pure and do no checks. Types already limit priority, but screens may pass untyped values at runtime.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Reject the four kinds of bad input with a clear message, leaving the list untouched.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Changing `untag`, `find` or filters; normalising tags (case, trimming); changing existing behaviour for valid input.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- New error code `invalid-input` in `TodoErrorCode`; distinct from `not-found`/`duplicate` so screens can tell it apart.
+- Validators `validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag` in `task.ts`, each returning `Result`, called by `list.ts` before any lookup or mutation. Validation runs first, so nothing (including the id counter) changes on rejection.
+- The title is trimmed before checking, matching how titles are already stored; the 120 limit applies to the trimmed title.
+- Tags are not trimmed: a tag with any space, including surrounding ones, is rejected.
+- Validation lives in the list methods, not in the pure helpers, to keep them unchanged.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Callers relying on blank titles or spaced tags now get errors; this is intended.
+- Existing `TodoErrorCode` switches in screens may need a new case.
