+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, so odd tasks get in: blank or huge titles, unknown priorities, empty or spaced tags. The list should refuse them with a clear error.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `add`, `rename` and `tag` reject: a title that is empty or only spaces; a title longer than 120 characters (after trimming); a priority other than `low`, `normal`, `high`; a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+- `add` also checks the tags it is given.
+- Rejection returns a new `invalid-input` error whose message says what is wrong; the list is left unchanged.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-input-validation`: which titles, priorities and tags the list accepts, and how it reports the rest.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/result.ts`: new `invalid-input` error code.
+- `src/domain/task.ts`: validation functions.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: `add`, `rename`, `tag` validate before changing anything.
+- `test/list.test.ts`: new tests. No new dependency.
